# Build outputs - the crew package ships a compiled exe, but it is assembled
# by the master at generate time, not committed here.
collector.exe
collector-master.exe

# Captures are session data. The rev 5 addendum is explicit that no captures\
# content may ever leave this machine in a crew package; keeping them out of
# git is the same rule applied to the repo.
captures/

# --auto runtime artifacts. Both are written NEXT TO THE EXE at run time and
# belong to whoever is running it, not to the repo:
#   collector-auto.log      what the unattended loop did, for hours at a time
#   collector-settings.txt  the user's own interval/poll choices, generated on
#                           first run. Committing it would push one machine's
#                           settings onto everyone else's.
collector-auto.log
collector-settings.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-install secrets and personal state. Added 2026-08-09, when the first
# commit of this directory in three days nearly took all of them with it.
#
# collector-scrub-salt.bin   THE IMPORTANT ONE. scrub.go:46 says the salt "is
#                            random per install and never leaves the machine",
#                            and the whole point of salting is that an unsalted
#                            hash of a handle is reversible. Committing this
#                            file would make every pseudonymised player name in
#                            every export reversible by anyone holding the repo.
#                            It is 32 bytes and it is the privacy guarantee.
# collector-install-id.txt   This machine's contributor id. Committing it would
#                            make one person's exports attributable, and would
#                            hand every clone the same id.
# collector-consent.txt      A record of a specific human agreeing to something,
#                            with a timestamp. Not repo content.
collector-scrub-salt.bin
collector-install-id.txt
collector-consent.txt

# Runtime markers and machine-specific output. Written next to the exe while it
# runs; they describe one machine's session, not the program.
collector-running.marker
collector-shortcut.txt
collector-selftest-results.txt
selftest-rerun-*.txt

# Packages are built by make-package.ps1 / make-release.ps1 from the source
# that IS committed. A 6 MB zip per release would bloat the history for
# something reproducible from a tag.
citizen-collector-*.zip
